cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Metalcyte in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Metalcyte: single-cell analysis on Apple silicon"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tran
    given-names: Thai Huu Loc
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1810-010X"
    affiliation: "Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Hong Hung Hospital, Tay Ninh City, Viet Nam"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/huulocmedvnu/metalcyte"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/metalcyte/"
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - scRNA-seq
  - Apple silicon
  - Metal
  - GPU
  - Rust
  - out-of-core
abstract: >-
  Metalcyte analyses single-cell RNA-seq data on Macs with Apple silicon. You call it from
  Python, and its calculations run in Rust. It runs
  preprocessing, PCA, neighbour graphs, UMAP, t-SNE, clustering and marker gene tests on the
  CPU cores, the chip's matrix unit and the GPU. It can also analyse datasets too large for
  the computer's memory, by reading the count matrix from disk in blocks.
